194
00:20:32,776 --> 00:20:38,276
憧れはそのままで 夢から目覚めた先には夢
My longing remains unchanged, and waking from a dream leads only to another dream.

195
00:20:38,376 --> 00:20:43,576
聞こえたその泣き声 消える手前のむせび散る哀れ
I heard that cry, a choking sorrow scattering just before it fades away.

196
00:20:43,676 --> 00:20:49,076
憧れのその先へ うずくまる君を見つけるため
Beyond that longing, to find you cowering there.

197
00:20:49,376 --> 00:20:52,776
行け 行け 追いつけない速度で
Go, go, at an unreachable speed,

198
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:55,576
飛べ インパルス加速して
Fly, accelerated by impulse,

199
00:20:55,676 --> 00:20:59,776
行け 居処を感じるために生まれてきたんだ
Go! I was born to feel where I belong.

200
00:20:59,876 --> 00:21:04,476
未来を掴んで 期待値を越えて 額に刺さる風
Seize the future, surpass expectations, with the wind piercing your forehead.

201
00:21:04,576 --> 00:21:10,076
今に見よ きっと君の眩しさに誰もが気づくだろう
Just wait and see, surely everyone will notice your brilliance soon.

202
00:21:10,776 --> 00:21:15,676
相応しい声で 視線追い越して 虚空を越えて行け
With a fitting voice, overtaking every gaze, cross through the void and go.

203
00:21:15,776 --> 00:21:21,576
見違えていく君の指から今 手を放す
From your transforming fingers, I now let go of your hand.

204
00:21:31,076 --> 00:21:36,576
気付けば謎は解かれ 宿命ごと見慣れた板の上
Before I realized it, the mystery was solved, along with fate, upon these familiar boards.

205
00:21:36,676 --> 00:21:41,376
あの頃焦がれたような 大人になれたかな
Have I become the adult I yearned to be back then?

206
00:21:41,576 --> 00:21:45,876
そう君の群青は 君が自分で選んだ旅だ
Yes, your deep blue is a journey you chose for yourself,

207
00:21:45,976 --> 00:21:51,376
そして掴んだのなら 誰も彼もすべて君のものだ
And if you've seized it, then everything and everyone belongs to you.

208
00:21:51,576 --> 00:21:56,076
僕の夢になって 弓を番えて 狙いを定めて
Becoming my dream, nock the arrow to the bow, take aim,

209
00:21:56,176 --> 00:22:00,876
強く引いた 今君は決して風になれない
And pull back hard; right now you can never become the wind.

210
00:22:00,976 --> 00:22:04,476
矢になって 行け
Become the arrow and go!

211
00:22:04,576 --> 00:22:06,876
飛べ 決して振り向かないで
Fly! Never look back!

212
00:22:06,976 --> 00:22:09,676
飛べ もう届かない場所へ
Fly to a place beyond reach!

213
00:22:09,776 --> 00:22:14,876
行け 行け 行け 君はいつだって輝いていた
Go, go, go, you were always shining!

214
00:22:24,976 --> 00:22:29,876
未来を掴んで 期待値を越えて 額に刺さる風
Seize the future, surpass expectations, with the wind piercing your forehead.

215
00:22:29,976 --> 00:22:35,476
今に見よ きっと君の眩しさに誰もが気づくだろう
Just wait and see, surely everyone will notice your brilliance soon.

216
00:22:35,576 --> 00:22:40,776
相応しい声で 視線追い越して 虚空を越えて行け
With a fitting voice, overtaking every gaze, cross through the void and go.

217
00:22:40,876 --> 00:22:47,276
見違えていく君の指から今 手を放す
From your transforming fingers, I now let go of your hand.

218
00:23:12,376 --> 00:23:24,076
はじめてのキッスは 涙の味がした
My first kiss tasted like tears,

219
00:23:24,876 --> 00:23:35,576
まるでドラマみたいな恋 見つからなかったように 灰色のベルが鳴る
Like a romance out of a drama, as if never found, the grey bell tolls...

220
00:23:47,076 --> 00:23:52,076
冷たい冬の風が 頬をかすめる
The cold winter wind grazes my cheek,

221
00:23:52,176 --> 00:23:58,376
吐いた白息で 両手を擦った
I rubbed my hands together with my white exhaled breath.

222
00:23:58,576 --> 00:24:03,076
街はイルミネーション 魔法をかけたみたい
The city is lit with illuminations, as if under a magic spell,

223
00:24:03,176 --> 00:24:08,076
裸の街灯がキラキラ
Bare streetlights shine brightly.

224
00:24:08,576 --> 00:24:12,376
悲しくても
Even though it was sad,

225
00:24:12,476 --> 00:24:18,576
嫌だった この気持ち抑えてきた
I hated it, suppressing these feelings...

226
00:24:18,776 --> 00:24:24,476
前から決めていた事だから これでいいの
Because it's something I decided long ago, this is for the best,

227
00:24:24,576 --> 00:24:28,576
ふたりはもう...
The two of us are no longer...

228
00:24:28,676 --> 00:24:30,376
知らない
Strangers.

229
00:24:30,476 --> 00:24:35,076
ありがとう さようなら 切ない片想い
Thank you, goodbye, my painful one-sided love.

230
00:24:35,176 --> 00:24:40,376
足をとめたら 思い出してしまう
If I stop in my tracks, I'll end up remembering.

231
00:24:40,476 --> 00:24:46,376
だから ありがとう さようなら 泣いたりしないから
So thank you, goodbye, I won't cry anymore.

232
00:24:46,576 --> 00:24:51,376
そう思った 途端にふわり
Just as I thought that, gently...

233
00:24:51,576 --> 00:24:58,576
舞い降りてくる雪 触れたら溶けて消えた
The fluttering snow melted and vanished the moment I touched it.

234
00:25:07,170 --> 00:25:10,970
粉雪続く大通り
On the main street where powder snow falls,

235
00:25:10,970 --> 00:25:14,870
寄り添ってる二人 楽しそう
a couple walks side-by-side, looking so happy.

236
00:25:14,870 --> 00:25:18,170
「ほら見て 初雪！」
"Look, the first snow!"

237
00:25:18,170 --> 00:25:22,170
君とあんな風になりたくて
Wanting to be like that with you,

238
00:25:22,170 --> 00:25:26,170
初めて作った
for the first time I knitted

239
00:25:26,170 --> 00:25:29,170
手編みのマフラー
a handmade scarf.

240
00:25:29,170 --> 00:25:32,470
どうしたら渡せたんだろう
How could I have given it to you?

241
00:25:32,470 --> 00:25:35,470
意気地なし
I was such a coward,

242
00:25:35,470 --> 00:25:38,870
怖かっただけ
just so scared.

243
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:41,670
思い出になるなら
If this is just going to become a memory,

244
00:25:41,670 --> 00:25:44,870
このままで構わないって
keeping things as they are would be fine, I said,

245
00:25:44,870 --> 00:25:50,470
それはほんとなの？
but is that really true?

246
00:25:50,470 --> 00:25:53,170
ありがとう サヨナラ
Thank you, goodbye.

247
00:25:53,170 --> 00:25:59,870
いつかこんな時が来てしまうこと
That a time like this would come eventually...

248
00:25:59,870 --> 00:26:00,870
なのに
...and yet...

249
00:26:00,870 --> 00:26:03,670
ありがとう サヨナラ
Thank you, goodbye.

250
00:26:03,670 --> 00:26:06,670
体が震えてる
My body is trembling.

251
00:26:06,670 --> 00:26:11,670
もうすぐ列車が来るのに
Even though the train is coming soon.

252
00:26:11,670 --> 00:26:16,670
それは今になって 私を苦しめる
Only now does it hurt me so much.

253
00:26:16,670 --> 00:26:20,670
繋がりたい
I want us to be connected.

254
00:26:20,670 --> 00:26:26,670
どれほど願っただろう
How much did I wish for it?

255
00:26:26,670 --> 00:26:29,670
この手は
These hands...

256
00:26:29,670 --> 00:26:32,670
空を切る
...reach out into empty air.

257
00:26:32,670 --> 00:26:36,670
ねぇ サヨナラって
Hey, saying goodbye...

258
00:26:36,670 --> 00:26:39,670
痛い
...hurts so much.

259
00:26:59,670 --> 00:27:01,870
行かなくちゃ
I have to go,

260
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:04,670
そんなの分かってる
I know that.

261
00:27:04,670 --> 00:27:10,170
君が優しいことも知ってる
I also know how kind you are.

262
00:27:10,170 --> 00:27:13,670
だから この手を離してよ
So please, let go of my hand.

263
00:27:13,670 --> 00:27:18,170
出会えてよかった
I'm glad I met you.

264
00:27:18,170 --> 00:27:20,670
君が好き
I love you.

265
00:27:20,670 --> 00:27:23,670
ありがとう サヨナラ
Thank you, goodbye.

266
00:27:23,670 --> 00:27:26,170
一言が言えない
I can't say those simple words.

267
00:27:26,170 --> 00:27:31,170
今だけでいい 私に勇気を
Just for now, give me courage.

268
00:27:31,170 --> 00:27:33,670
「解けて」
"Melt away,"

269
00:27:33,670 --> 00:27:36,670
かじかんだ手 君との距離はゼロ
my frozen hand... The distance between us is zero.

270
00:27:36,670 --> 00:27:41,670
今だけは泣いていいよね
It's okay to cry just for now, right?

271
00:27:41,670 --> 00:27:44,670
もう言葉はいらない
No more words are needed.

272
00:27:44,670 --> 00:27:49,670
お願い ギュッとしてて
Please, just hold me tight.

273
00:27:58,670 --> 00:28:04,670
来年の今頃には
By this time next year,

274
00:28:04,670 --> 00:28:07,170
どんな私がい(て)
what kind of person will I be,

275
00:28:07,170 --> 00:28:11,670
どんな君がいるのかな
and what kind of person will you be?

276
00:28:31,170 --> 00:28:33,170
Wow, you got some extensions!

277
00:28:33,170 --> 00:28:34,870
Extensions? I don't remember getting anything like that.

278
00:28:34,870 --> 00:28:37,170
Your hair is even longer!

279
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:39,870
Heh, it's fashionable, though, don't you think?

280
00:28:39,870 --> 00:28:41,470
It looks kind of familiar.

281
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:43,470
Hm... Like maybe we're missing something... Oh!

282
00:28:43,470 --> 00:28:45,870
Oh, you have another arm, too?

283
00:28:45,870 --> 00:28:47,670
Whoa, there. Hold on a second, something's...

284
00:28:47,670 --> 00:28:49,470
You're growing, huh?

285
00:28:49,470 --> 00:28:50,670
Not only has the season changed...

286
00:28:50,670 --> 00:28:52,670
I lost count!

287
00:28:52,670 --> 00:28:55,670
Wait, it looks like we've lost somebody... Welcome back!

288
00:28:55,670 --> 00:28:57,470
Hi! Hello!

289
00:28:57,470 --> 00:28:59,670
You're here, you're here! Ina, nice hair!

290
00:28:59,670 --> 00:29:01,670
Oh, thank you.

291
00:29:01,670 --> 00:29:03,670
The seasons have changed.

292
00:29:03,670 --> 00:29:06,170
Yes, it's getting a little warmer, thank goodness.

293
00:29:06,170 --> 00:29:11,170
It was kind of cool, you know? It was a little chilly...

294
00:29:11,170 --> 00:29:14,470
Spring! Yay! So beautiful!

295
00:29:14,470 --> 00:29:17,470
Yeah, check it out. The stage is so pink!

296
00:29:17,470 --> 00:29:20,170
I actually really like the color pink now after these six years.

297
00:29:20,170 --> 00:29:23,670
Character development! That's good, that's good.

298
00:29:23,670 --> 00:29:28,170
And we're wearing yukata, kimono, whatever you want it to be!

299
00:29:28,170 --> 00:29:29,870
And we all went for kind of a blue color, yeah?

300
00:29:29,870 --> 00:29:31,670
Yeah, we do look like we're about to drop a sweet enka album.

301
00:29:31,670 --> 00:29:35,170
Isn't this how they pose?

302
00:29:35,170 --> 00:29:38,670
どっこいしょ、どっこいしょ！ どっこいしょ、どっこいしょ！
Dokkoisho, dokkoisho! Dokkoisho, dokkoisho!

303
00:29:38,670 --> 00:29:42,870
ソーラン、ソーラン！ ソーラン、ソーラン！ ヤーレン、ソーラン！
Soran, soran! Soran, soran! Yaren, soran!

304
00:29:42,870 --> 00:29:46,670
Okay, that's not what we're doing! We're not releasing that!

305
00:29:46,670 --> 00:29:48,670
So we did a bunch of songs...

306
00:29:48,670 --> 00:29:50,870
Like, for example?

307
00:29:50,870 --> 00:29:54,170
For example, "Step and Step"... That's not that one!

308
00:29:54,170 --> 00:29:57,170
That you sang! No, please!

309
00:29:57,170 --> 00:30:02,670
But this is a really iconic old Japanese song, okay?

310
00:30:06,396 --> 00:30:09,596
It was so cute. I hope you guys enjoyed this cover too.

311
00:30:09,896 --> 00:30:11,096
Yeah. Right?

312
00:30:11,296 --> 00:30:13,396
Yeah, Ina, did you know it before?

313
00:30:13,496 --> 00:30:14,096
No.

314
00:30:14,196 --> 00:30:15,896
No? Calli, did you know it before?

315
00:30:15,996 --> 00:30:18,596
No. First time hearing it?

316
00:30:18,696 --> 00:30:22,596
I think everyone in the chat will also, when they hear the word September...
I think everyone in the chat, when they hear the word "September"...

317
00:30:22,896 --> 00:30:24,996
No, no, no! That's a different song!

318
00:30:25,096 --> 00:30:27,896
No, this is how we change the impression of September!

319
00:30:27,996 --> 00:30:32,596
When we say September, you don't think of that September, you think about this September with me and Ina, okay?

320
00:30:32,896 --> 00:30:34,196
Yeah, it's just for now.

321
00:30:34,396 --> 00:30:36,496
Yeah! What else did we perform?

322
00:30:36,896 --> 00:30:40,596
Oh, I also saw you did some ballet skating moves.

323
00:30:40,896 --> 00:30:43,996
Are you a filthy archer? I'm disgusted.

324
00:30:44,096 --> 00:30:46,296
You hate archers? I hate archers.

325
00:30:46,396 --> 00:30:50,796
But Genshin... They're such cheaters!

326
00:30:50,896 --> 00:30:53,896
I've never seen this anime, but is there actually an archer in there?

327
00:30:53,996 --> 00:30:55,296
Yeah. Wait, really? No.

328
00:30:55,596 --> 00:30:57,996
Oh, no! There are skaters, though.

329
00:30:58,196 --> 00:31:01,696
Oh! Figure skaters. That's not a skate!

330
00:31:01,896 --> 00:31:04,696
Oh, I can! I can do it. I'm all right.

331
00:31:04,796 --> 00:31:08,296
I can skate too. Okay! Really? We should go, we should go!

332
00:31:08,396 --> 00:31:11,196
I can ice skate! That was my favorite hobby when I was younger.

333
00:31:11,296 --> 00:31:12,896
It's a promise.

334
00:31:13,096 --> 00:31:17,596
Anyway, I loved your low tones. - Yes, thank you. - It was really hot.

335
00:31:18,096 --> 00:31:21,396
No, no, no, it came out beautifully. You sounded wonderful.

336
00:31:21,696 --> 00:31:25,096
Thank you! And I got to sing with Kiara as the snow fell.

337
00:31:25,296 --> 00:31:29,196
We talked and sang a song about first love... - It was super cute.

338
00:31:29,296 --> 00:31:33,896
Weren't we so cute? - It's just what happens when first love ends...

339
00:31:34,096 --> 00:31:38,096
Takamori! So, it feels wholesome to me, I don't know.

340
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:44,896
君に決めて... Mwa, mwa, no kissu! Mwa, mwa, mwa! Kissu.
I choose you... Mwa, mwa, kisses! Mwa, mwa, mwa! Kisses.

341
00:31:45,096 --> 00:31:48,896
How did that make you feel, everybody in the chat?

342
00:31:48,996 --> 00:31:51,896
Were you jealous, or were you happy for us?

343
00:31:52,096 --> 00:31:54,096
Think carefully about your answer.

344
00:31:54,296 --> 00:31:56,596
Were you happy for us? - Totally, okay. Thank you.

345
00:31:57,096 --> 00:32:00,596
They're definitely saying yes. - Yay!

346
00:32:00,896 --> 00:32:05,096
Well, we have also changed costume. - Yes.

347
00:32:05,196 --> 00:32:07,596
Blue! We're so blue!

348
00:32:07,696 --> 00:32:11,596
White and pink. White, blue, pink... Red, white, and...

349
00:32:11,696 --> 00:32:13,596
Red, white, and blue!

350
00:32:13,696 --> 00:32:17,596
Not quite. Goldfish, Kingyo, and... Mizu-iro.
Not quite. Goldfish, Kingyo, and... light blue.

351
00:32:17,696 --> 00:32:20,896
'Cause I got purple purps.

352
00:32:21,096 --> 00:32:23,096
あー、そうだね。
Ah, that's right.

353
00:32:23,196 --> 00:32:26,096
Wait, is this morning glory?

354
00:32:26,296 --> 00:32:28,896
Ah, I thought they were jellyfish. - Are they jellyfish?

355
00:32:29,096 --> 00:32:31,596
No, I think it's morning... morning glory!

356
00:32:31,696 --> 00:32:37,296
It could also be Austrian bread! That's exactly the shape of Austrian bread!

357
00:32:37,396 --> 00:32:39,596
Do the breads come in those colors?

358
00:32:39,696 --> 00:32:43,096
No! Well, maybe if they're moldy!

359
00:32:43,196 --> 00:32:47,996
Ara ara! Hope you never eat one of those! Don't eat moldy bread!

360
00:32:48,096 --> 00:32:53,096
Have you eaten moldy bread before, everybody? No? Are you sure?

361
00:32:53,196 --> 00:32:57,996
Stale, stale bread. Why is this what we're talking about during our concert?

362
00:32:58,096 --> 00:33:00,596
It's okay. A little whimsy is fine.

363
00:33:00,696 --> 00:33:06,096
But now how about we get serious for a moment and sing a song... a曲, song.
But now how about we get serious for a moment and sing a song... a song, song.

364
00:33:06,196 --> 00:33:09,596
Shut up! Stop it!

365
00:33:09,696 --> 00:33:14,596
Let's sing a song that's a little bit emoi. I was listening to the lyrics and practicing it...
Let's sing a song that's a little bit emotional. I was listening to the lyrics and practicing it...

366
00:33:14,696 --> 00:33:18,596
...and I was like, "Hmm, you know, there are a couple lyrics here and there..."

367
00:33:18,696 --> 00:33:22,596
"...that remind me of the struggles that we have gone through, and how I want to go forward with you guys."

368
00:33:22,696 --> 00:33:28,096
So it made me kind of like, "Ah, emoi." So I hope we can sing it well together.
So it made me kind of like, "Ah, emotional." So I hope we can sing it well together.

369
00:33:28,196 --> 00:33:34,596
We will! We will! And let's do it in these slightly restrictive...

370
00:33:34,696 --> 00:33:37,296
But they're really stretchy! Okay! All right, enough of that!

371
00:33:37,396 --> 00:33:40,096
You like that. Don't do that.

372
00:33:41,096 --> 00:33:45,596
Positions! Now we start. Now we dance and sing.

373
00:33:45,696 --> 00:33:49,596
All right, listen to our next song: "Suzume".

374
00:34:32,896 --> 00:34:39,396
君の中にある 赤と青き線
The red and blue lines inside of you,

375
00:34:39,596 --> 00:34:45,096
それらが結ばれるのは 心の臓
the place where they are bound is the heart.

376
00:34:45,596 --> 00:34:51,096
風の中でも 負けないような声で
With a voice that won't lose even to the wind,

377
00:34:51,296 --> 00:34:57,096
届ける言葉を 今は育ててる
I am now nurturing the words to deliver to you.

378
00:34:57,296 --> 00:35:03,096
時はまくらぎ 風はにかはだ
Time is a sleeper, the wind is bare skin,

379
00:35:04,140 --> 00:35:06,340
...うぶすな
...guardian deity,

380
00:35:06,340 --> 00:35:09,840
人はかげろう
human life is a fleeting mirage.

381
00:35:09,940 --> 00:35:14,940
「なんで泣いてるの？」と聞かれ答えれる
When asked why I'm crying, if I can answer...

382
00:35:14,940 --> 00:35:21,440
涙なんかじゃ 僕が出会えたことの意味にはまるで
...tears alone couldn't possibly do justice...

383
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:25,140
追いつかない
...to the meaning of us meeting.

384
00:35:25,140 --> 00:35:28,740
この身ひとつじゃ 足りない叫び
With just this body, my cries are not enough.

385
00:35:28,740 --> 00:35:33,040
君の手触れた時にだけ震えた
Only when I touched your hand did it tremble...

386
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:35,140
心があったよ
...a heart was truly there.

387
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:39,040
意味をいくつ越えれば僕らはたどり
How many meanings must we cross...

388
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:41,140
